# D1: the AUDITED arm of lever D2, run before the timing pair TW1-TW4. c2-packed-tp4-gate-draftwide is c2-packed-tp4-gate (every verify audit ON) plus
# QWEN_FAST_TP4_DRAFT_WIDE=1 and nothing else. Why it exists: draft_wide_tp allocates width-sharded L1 buffers INSIDE the drafter pair traces, which are captured lazily,
# after the verify captures; before this lever the drafter used no L1. A persistent L1 buffer allocated after the first drafter capture can land on the freed shard
# addresses and be overwritten by every drafter replay, which would corrupt target state or hang the audits-off timing arms with nothing to show where. The T1 and T2 audits
# compare the packed trace's sampler and verify rows in place, so a corruption shows here as a mismatch line. The matrix runs four users at 4,096 / 16,384 / 32,768 / 60,000
# prompt tokens, 512 out, every user's text against the same user alone.
# Read: POLICY PASS and every user identical to solo; no audit mismatch line; the engine log shows '[PINDIAG] tp4 draft wide engaged' and no 'fell back' line.
# A FAIL here (or a hang) means the lever writes over live L1: SKIP TW1-TW4 and do not time the lever until its buffers are allocated before any capture.
# OPTIONAL: a failure does not stop the window (it decides whether the draftwide pair runs). Duration (estimate): 60-120 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/next-3-cheap window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: the one fresh tag B0 builds; C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3m is a PLACEHOLDER the driver substitutes in every template.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate-draftwide
C2_GATE_PLAN=matrix
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=4096,16384,32768,60000
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=512
C2_GATE_JIT=record
